Machine Learning for P2P Lending Risk
A machine learning pipeline for credit-risk scoring and default prediction on large-scale P2P lending data.

Project Overview
This project focuses on assessing credit risk in peer-to-peer (P2P) lending platforms. 
As a group project, I led the data preparation and core predictive modeling phases, building robust algorithms to identify potential borrower defaults and support risk-management decisions.

Key Responsibilities & Contributions
Data Preprocessing & Feature Engineering: Handled large-scale lending datasets, performed data cleaning, addressed missing values, and engineered predictive features relevant to credit scoring.

Model Development: Designed and trained credit-risk scoring and default-prediction models using advanced machine learning algorithms, specifically LightGBM and Random Forest.

Optimization & Evaluation: Conducted rigorous hyperparameter tuning to optimize model performance and performed feature-importance analysis to interpret risk drivers.
